": "specialist"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high-level"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "specialized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hospital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AAA"}]}, {"id": "body-22132", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "AAAs are usually treated with surgical repair in ruptured, symptomatic or appropriately sized aneurysms. When indicated, unruptured aneurysms can undergo elective repair Newer minimally invasive techniques extend aortic aneurysm treatment into an increasingly elderly population. Recommend elective repair for the patient at low or acceptable surgical risk with a fusiform AAA that is ≥5.5 cm in males and >5cm in females.", "runs": [{"text": "AAAs are usually treated with surgical repair in ruptured, symptomatic or appropriately sized aneurysms. When indicated, unruptured aneurysms can undergo elective repair Newer minimally invasive techniques extend aortic aneurysm treatment into an increasingly elderly population. Recommend elective repair for the patient at low or acceptable surgical risk with a fusiform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AAA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that is ≥5.5 cm in males and >5cm in females."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "677"}}, {"id": "body-22133", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "If an AAA ruptures, emergency surgical repair is required. The primary repair methods are as follows:", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AAA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ruptures,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "emergency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "repair"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "required."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "repair"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "methods"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "follows:"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "677"}}, {"id": "body-22134", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Open - This requires direct access to the aorta via a transperitoneal or retroperitoneal approach", "runs": [{"text": "Open"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "This"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "requires"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "direct"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "access"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aorta"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "via"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transperitoneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "retroperitoneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "approach"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "677"}}, {"id": "body-22135", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Endovascular - This involves gaining access to the lumen of the abdominal aorta, usually via the femoral vessels; an endograft, typically a polyester or Gore-Tex graft with a stent exoskeleton, is placed within the lumen of the AAA, extending distally into the iliac arteries", "runs": [{"text": "Endovascular - This involves gaining access to the lumen of the abdominal aorta, usually via the femoral vessels; an endograft, typically a polyester or Gore-Tex graft with a stent exoskeleton, is placed within the lumen of the AAA, extending distally into the iliac arteries"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "677"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Cardiovascular disease conditions", "start": "body-22117", "end": "body-22135"}}